  """
// Section 12 (Branching, Distribution, and the Canopy).
//
// Definition 12.1 (Branch Point): a resolution with multiple
// coherent outcomes.
//
// Theorem 12.2 (Structural Resolution at Branch Points):
// Selection among coherent outcomes is resolved structurally.
// Each outcome B_i has persistence magnitude p_i.
// Each outcome's share: p_i^2 / p_total^2 (quadratic, from
// Pythagorean conservation). Where outcomes are structurally
// equivalent, selection is uniformly random.
//
// Probability is a structural quantity, determined by the geometry
// of the branch point itself.
//
// Definition 12.3 (Branching): production of multiple coherent
// outcomes. From within a trace, branching appears as selection.
// From the canopy, all coherent outcomes are actualized.
//
// Definition 12.4 (Trace): one sequence of branch selections.
// One path through the chain of resolutions.
//
// Derives from: theory.forcing.collapse, theory.mixing.pythagorean
  """
}
